From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:02:58 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Add a setup switch for the Intel display
 audio

The HD Audio controller at 0:3.0 carries the audio of the digital
display ports of the iGPU. On the W541 the iGPU drives the panel and
the VGA port, neither with audio, so its codec has nothing to drive.
Under macOS AppleHDAHDMI_DPDriver still powers that codec at every wake,
and at sleep with the display already off, and waits 10 s for an answer
each time: the wake takes 10-20 s instead of about 1.3 s, and the
battery polling of SMCBatteryManager waits with it.

Add Hardware > Graphics > "Intel display audio", on by default as the
OEM firmware has it. Off, the mainboard marks 0:3.0 disabled before
enumeration and disable_devices() of the northbridge clears DEVEN.D3EN,
at boot and at S3 resume: no OS sees the controller. The HDAU device
of the DSDT stays, as an _ADR with no function behind it.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init; the
option and its text are in the ramstage.

Co-authored-by: Claude Fable 5.1 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c       | 13 +++++++++++++
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 29 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index 2f40c0734a..9698319f60 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -543,6 +543,18 @@ static const struct sm_object thunderbolt = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
 	.default_value	= true,
 });
 
+/* The HD Audio controller for the digital display ports of the iGPU, 0:3.0 */
+static const struct sm_object minihd_audio = SM_DECLARE_BOOL({
+	.flags		= CONFIG(BOARD_LENOVO_THINKPAD_W541) ? 0 : CFR_OPTFLAG_SUPPRESS,
+	.opt_name	= "minihd_audio",
+	.ui_name	= "Intel display audio",
+	.ui_helptext	= "The audio controller of the display ports of the Intel GPU.\n"
+			  "On the W541 the Intel GPU drives the panel and the VGA port,\n"
+			  "neither with audio. Disabled: the controller is hidden, and\n"
+			  "an OS does not wait for its codec at every wake (macOS).",
+	.default_value	= true,
+});
+
 static const struct sm_object hardware_graphics = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Graphics",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
@@ -554,6 +566,7 @@ static const struct sm_object hardware_graphics = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 		&gfx_aperture_size,
 		&gfx_fb_limit,
 		&gfx_resume_init,
+		&minihd_audio,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
index 0c55fa7177..66d4a0c7fd 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/mainboard.c
@@ -120,6 +120,22 @@ static void mainboard_enable(struct device *dev)
 			disable_root_port(2, "ExpressCard");
 		if (!get_uint_option("thunderbolt", 1))
 			disable_root_port(4, "Thunderbolt");
+
+		/*
+		 * The Intel display audio controller, 0:3.0: the iGPU of the W541
+		 * drives the panel and the VGA port, neither with audio. Off, the
+		 * northbridge clears its DEVEN bit (disable_devices()), at boot
+		 * and at S3 resume: no OS sees it.
+		 */
+		if (!get_uint_option("minihd_audio", 1)) {
+			struct device *minihd = pcidev_on_root(0x03, 0);
+
+			if (minihd && minihd->enabled) {
+				printk(BIOS_INFO, "Intel display audio: disabling %s\n",
+				       dev_path(minihd));
+				minihd->enabled = 0;
+			}
+		}
 	}
 }
 
